WEBVTT

00:01.020 --> 00:05.520
<i>Reigning champions Nankatsu finally catch up during the second half.</i>

00:06.100 --> 00:09.960
<i>They've scored an important goal thanks to the center-back Takasugi's efforts.</i>

00:09.960 --> 00:12.530
<i>Can Nankatsu keep this up and turn the tables?</i>

00:12.530 --> 00:18.530
<i>On the other hand, we have the first time contender Azumaichi MS putting up a great show despite being caught up!</i>

00:18.530 --> 00:21.470
<i>Can they maintain the tie and go to the penalty shootout?</i>

00:21.470 --> 00:22.500
<i>You fool.</i>

00:22.500 --> 00:24.010
<i>A tie is out of the question.</i>

00:24.010 --> 00:25.790
<i>We'll win and show you!</i>

00:26.320 --> 00:29.130
<i>There are just 10 minutes left in the second half.</i>

00:29.640 --> 00:34.180
<i>The match will be decided by just one more goal!</i>

00:36.180 --> 00:39.010
<i>Soda won't let it end like this.</i>

00:41.270 --> 00:43.980
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

00:41.270 --> 00:43.980
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

00:44.890 --> 00:47.560
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

00:44.890 --> 00:47.560
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

00:48.480 --> 00:51.190
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

00:48.480 --> 00:51.190
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

00:58.070 --> 01:00.910
<i>moeru you ni hitori demo</i>

00:58.070 --> 01:00.910
<i>I keep running, lying to myself</i>

01:00.910 --> 01:07.170
<i>ikiteyukeru to usobuite hashiritsudzukete</i>

01:00.910 --> 01:07.170
<i>that I can live alone, though the loneliness makes me burn</i>

01:07.170 --> 01:13.050
<i>unubore no morosa wo kimi wa shitteta na no ni</i>

01:07.170 --> 01:13.050
<i>You knew how fragile my self-conceit makes me</i>

01:13.050 --> 01:19.640
<i>kokoro made uchinomaresareta kono yoru ni</i>

01:13.050 --> 01:19.640
<i>In this night that even shattered my heart</i>

01:19.640 --> 01:23.640
<i>kimi no koe sagasu</i>

01:19.640 --> 01:23.640
<i>I hate how weak I am</i>

01:23.640 --> 01:28.150
<i>kono yowasa ga nikui yo</i>

01:23.640 --> 01:28.150
<i>yearning for your voice</i>

01:28.150 --> 01:33.690
<i>ima sugu torimodoshi ni ikanakya</i>

01:28.150 --> 01:33.690
<i>"I've got to get you back right now!"</i>

01:33.690 --> 01:35.280
<i>baka darou?</i>

01:33.690 --> 01:35.280
<i>I'm stupid, right?</i>

01:35.280 --> 01:36.490
<i>ai</i>

01:35.280 --> 01:36.490
<i>Love!</i>

01:36.490 --> 01:39.990
<i>kizudarake no ai wo shinjite</i>

01:36.490 --> 01:39.990
<i>Believing in my scarred love</i>

01:39.990 --> 01:49.880
<i>nagareochita namida sae mo tsuyosa e to kaete</i>

01:39.990 --> 01:49.880
<i>I will turn these shedded tears into strength</i>

01:49.880 --> 01:50.710
<i>ai</i>

01:49.880 --> 01:50.710
<i>Love!</i>

01:50.710 --> 01:54.510
<i>kizudarake no ai da to shite mo</i>

01:50.710 --> 01:54.510
<i>Even though it is a scarred love</i>

01:54.510 --> 01:58.510
<i>bokura no sekai wo tomoshiteru</i>

01:54.510 --> 01:58.510
<i>it lightens up our world</i>

01:58.510 --> 02:04.770
<i>kono ai mo ichido taritomo</i>

01:58.510 --> 02:04.770
<i>I will not let go of this love</i>

02:04.770 --> 02:07.560
<i>hanasanai</i>

02:04.770 --> 02:07.560
<i>for a single moment!</i>

02:09.190 --> 02:13.570
<b><b>EPISODE 36:
EACH ONE'S RESOLUTION</b></b>

02:09.810 --> 02:11.990
<i>The game resumes!</i>

02:13.780 --> 02:15.780
All right, everyone go!

02:15.780 --> 02:16.780
Yeah!

02:16.780 --> 02:21.810
<i>Despite having focused on defense so far, all Azumaichi players move onto the offensive!</i>

02:21.810 --> 02:23.030
Come at us if you will!

02:23.030 --> 02:26.290
<i>Both teams struggle to break away with the ball in the midfield!</i>

02:26.290 --> 02:30.500
<i>Soda himself continues to closely mark Tsubasa!</i>

02:34.550 --> 02:36.670
<i>Azumaichi fiercely attacks!</i>

02:36.670 --> 02:38.490
<i>However, Nankatsu fights back!</i>

02:38.490 --> 02:41.340
<i>The game is about to reach its climax!</i>

02:41.340 --> 02:42.970
Don't lose, Nankatsu!

02:42.970 --> 02:44.930
Go, Azumaichi!

02:47.430 --> 02:49.390
<i>Nankatsu just stole the ball!</i>

02:49.960 --> 02:51.660
All right, is Tsubasa open...

02:53.800 --> 02:55.600
Come on, Iwami!

02:55.600 --> 02:56.150
Okay!

02:56.840 --> 02:59.220
<i>Nankatsu gets the ball to Izawa.</i>

02:59.220 --> 03:01.710
<i>Will he make the game instead of Tsubasa?</i>

03:01.710 --> 03:02.950
Go, Taki!

03:02.950 --> 03:05.660
<i>Izawa decides to use Taki in the front lines.</i>

03:05.660 --> 03:06.790
I won't let this through!

03:06.790 --> 03:07.500
What?!

03:07.500 --> 03:09.370
It's my turn now!

03:09.370 --> 03:10.620
Guys, fall back!

03:10.620 --> 03:12.420
<i>Azumaichi's attack comes in like waves!</i>

03:14.280 --> 03:15.960
<i>But Kisugi cuts in!</i>

03:15.960 --> 03:16.920
Tsubasa!

03:16.920 --> 03:20.680
<i>Still, Tsubasa remains closely marked by Soda!</i>

03:21.760 --> 03:27.100
<i>Neither team is able to find an opening, and time continues ticking away!</i>

03:27.100 --> 03:29.180
<i>We just have 5 minutes left!</i>

03:31.540 --> 03:32.520
Here!

03:32.520 --> 03:34.630
<i>Ishizaki clears the loose ball.</i>

03:34.630 --> 03:37.360
<i>Azumaichi's attack has once again been blocked.</i>

03:38.110 --> 03:40.570
<i>The real game starts now! Let's go!</i>

03:40.570 --> 03:42.110
Oh no!

03:42.110 --> 03:46.780
<i>Soda leaves his mark on Tsubasa and chases after the cleared ball!</i>

03:47.160 --> 03:48.970
<i>Soda is closing in on the ball!</i>

03:48.970 --> 03:51.540
<i>But here's Nankatsu's Taki, challenging him for it!</i>

03:51.540 --> 03:53.650
Taki, I'm counting on you!

03:53.650 --> 03:54.170
All right!

03:54.170 --> 03:55.210
Eat this!

03:56.140 --> 03:57.880
Razor Tackle!

03:59.880 --> 04:03.300
<i>Soda steals the ball and proceeds to attack by himself!</i>

04:03.300 --> 04:06.140
<i>It feels like Azumaichi's about to score!</i>

04:06.140 --> 04:07.760
Morisaki, he's gonna shoot!

04:07.760 --> 04:10.270
Watch out for his shot's spin!

04:10.270 --> 04:10.850
Got it!

04:13.900 --> 04:14.690
<i>Tsubasa...</i>

04:15.360 --> 04:18.070
<i>Your Drive Shot is still incomplete.</i>

04:18.770 --> 04:23.150
<i>However, my Razor Shot is 100% complete!</i>

04:27.160 --> 04:29.660
<i>And this razor works both ways!</i>

04:30.070 --> 04:32.660
<i>We've got this game!</i>

04:35.360 --> 04:36.560
Morisaki, the other way!

04:36.560 --> 04:38.540
Jump to the opposite side this time!

04:41.560 --> 04:45.220
<i>Soda fires away his Razor Shot, which has already scored once!</i>

04:45.950 --> 04:48.190
<i>The way the ball spins now is different.</i>

04:48.190 --> 04:49.850
<i>It's headed to the left!</i>

04:49.850 --> 04:52.060
<i>It's a Reverse Razor Shot!</i>

04:54.120 --> 04:55.840
<i>H-he caught it!</i>

04:55.840 --> 04:58.140
<i>Morisaki firmly catches it this time.</i>

04:58.140 --> 04:59.480
<i>That's a great save!</i>

05:00.400 --> 05:01.420
Morisaki!

05:01.420 --> 05:03.150
You did it! Nice catch!

05:03.810 --> 05:05.660
All right! Come on, Morisaki!

05:07.410 --> 05:08.620
Okay! Tsubasa!

05:08.620 --> 05:12.790
<i>Since Soda has come forward to attack, Tsubasa is completely unmarked!</i>

05:12.790 --> 05:13.540
All right!

05:13.540 --> 05:17.710
<i>Azumaichi staged an attack with all of its players,
which has left them flat-footed on defense!</i>

05:17.710 --> 05:19.170
Crap! Go back!

05:19.170 --> 05:21.090
Go, Tsubasa!

05:21.090 --> 05:23.950
<i>Tsubasa is unmarked for the first time in this match.</i>

05:23.950 --> 05:26.240
<i>He's playing freely for the first time this game!</i>

05:26.240 --> 05:28.180
<i>Tsubasa, your leg...</i>

05:28.180 --> 05:29.610
<i>I'm unmarked.</i>

05:29.610 --> 05:33.770
<i>If I can't score now, there's no way we'll get our V3!</i>

05:35.390 --> 05:39.270
<i>Tsubasa beats the last defender, and heads straight to the goal!</i>

05:39.270 --> 05:41.960
<i>It's useless, no one can stop him now!</i>

05:45.380 --> 05:46.810
<i>Goal!</i>

05:46.810 --> 05:49.000
<i>It's Tsubasa's first goal in this tournament!</i>

05:49.000 --> 05:51.120
<i>And it's a goal for the win!</i>

05:51.120 --> 05:51.810
All right!

05:51.810 --> 05:52.540
I did it!

05:52.540 --> 05:54.310
<i>Nankatsu gets ahead!</i>

05:54.310 --> 06:02.300
<i>In the eleventh hour, right before the game ends, Captain Tsubasa scores the last-minute goal that may lift his team to victory!</i>

06:02.300 --> 06:03.860
You did it, Tsubasa!

06:03.860 --> 06:05.840
We have the lead!

06:05.840 --> 06:07.920
You made us worry for nothing!

06:07.920 --> 06:10.050
You went ahead and did it, Tsubasa!

06:10.050 --> 06:12.560
Well, everything should be fine with this.

06:13.160 --> 06:15.320
<i>How did he know?</i>

06:15.320 --> 06:17.980
<i>I haven't used my Reverse Razor Shot in the prelims...</i>

06:17.980 --> 06:21.270
<i>I hadn't even used it once... And yet...</i>

06:24.780 --> 06:27.530
<i>The final whistle blows!</i>

06:27.530 --> 06:32.280
<i>Azumaichi fought until the very end, but unfortunately for them, time is up!</i>

06:32.850 --> 06:34.280
<i>The score is 2-1!</i>

06:34.280 --> 06:39.590
<i>The reigning champion, Nankatsu MS clears the first game with some struggles, and advances to the second game.</i>

06:39.590 --> 06:43.290
<i>Whew...! We somehow got this first game.</i>

06:43.290 --> 06:45.960
<i>Azumachi won't see results for their efforts.</i>

06:45.960 --> 06:48.550
<i>But they've put up a good fight against Nankatsu.</i>

06:49.170 --> 06:50.740
<i>Well done, boys.</i>

06:50.740 --> 06:52.050
<i>It can't be helped.</i>

06:52.630 --> 06:55.680
<i>You did well as the Osaka representative, Soda.</i>

06:55.680 --> 07:00.770
Tsubasa Ozora... You really can't leave him unmarked, y'know.

07:00.770 --> 07:02.330
You're right.

07:02.330 --> 07:06.570
If Soda kept on marking Tsubasa instead of trying to take the lead,

07:06.570 --> 07:09.030
this game might have remained a tie.

07:09.030 --> 07:12.660
Well, it looks like it'll be us who beat Nankatsu.

07:12.660 --> 07:13.530
Yeah.

07:16.540 --> 07:17.710
Tsubasa.

07:18.290 --> 07:19.790
Soda...

07:19.790 --> 07:23.750
How did you read my Reverse Razor Shot?

07:23.750 --> 07:28.550
Good question. If Tsubasa didn't tell me what to do, I probably wouldn't get that one.

07:28.550 --> 07:31.380
It might just be a hunch on my part,

07:32.720 --> 07:36.430
when I looked at the angle between your pivot foot and shooting foot, I just knew.

07:36.430 --> 07:37.890
You "just knew"...

07:38.280 --> 07:42.520
You see, I'm having a hard time with curving the ball.

07:43.890 --> 07:45.490
I see.

07:45.490 --> 07:51.230
I'll most likely be unable to do it, so perfect your Drive Shot.

07:51.230 --> 07:53.090
I'm sure you can do it.

07:53.090 --> 07:54.280
Sure.

07:54.280 --> 07:57.370
Also, is your leg okay?

07:57.370 --> 07:59.660
His leg? Did something happen, Tsubasa?

07:59.660 --> 08:03.200
Tsubasa hurt his left leg a little. Really?

08:03.200 --> 08:05.180
It's okay.

08:05.180 --> 08:09.700
It's always acted up a bit, anyway.

08:09.700 --> 08:10.760
Well, that's fine, then.

08:11.800 --> 08:16.840
You have completely defeated us. Make sure you become the champions, Nankatsu.

08:16.840 --> 08:18.640
Yeah, just trust us.

08:19.080 --> 08:22.480
Well then... See you again, Tsubasa.

08:22.480 --> 08:25.400
Damn it! We just lost!

08:25.400 --> 08:27.360
Don't just feel down and cry, guys.

08:27.360 --> 08:28.970
Let's go home with our heads held high!

08:28.970 --> 08:30.230
Soda...

08:30.230 --> 08:32.230
Makoto Soda...

08:32.230 --> 08:36.490
I thought he was a pain in the ass, but it looks like he's actually a pretty cool guy.

08:40.900 --> 08:43.500
Nankatsu won, but they had a hard time.

08:43.500 --> 08:44.610
You're right.

08:44.610 --> 08:49.710
Can we acknowledge Soda, who marked Tsubasa, as a rival?

08:50.330 --> 08:51.960
You have a point.

08:51.960 --> 08:55.340
So, about that shot Tsubasa fired...

08:56.400 --> 09:00.060
Did he aim for it? Or was it just...

09:00.060 --> 09:02.980
Of course that was intentional.

09:02.980 --> 09:06.940
It's the Drive Shot that Tsubasa is in the process of developing right now.

09:06.940 --> 09:08.730
Drive Shot?

09:08.730 --> 09:20.560
Yes. If he were to 100% complete that shot, we could use Tsubasa in the Japanese National Team right now.

09:23.760 --> 09:25.790
<i>There's no doubt about it.</i>

09:25.790 --> 09:30.960
<i>This is clearly a Drive Shot that we see in South America, especially in Brazil.</i>

09:30.960 --> 09:33.710
<i>That shot is hard, even for the pros.</i>

09:33.710 --> 09:37.090
<i>Mastering that one in his 3rd year of middle school, albeit slowly...</i>

09:37.840 --> 09:42.350
<i>Tsubasa Ozora really is a guy people should fear.</i>

09:43.700 --> 09:45.850
<i>5 minutes of the second half have passed.</i>

09:45.850 --> 09:49.100
<i>It's the first match of the National Middle School Football Tournament</i>

09:49.100 --> 09:51.650
Fight! Fight! Toho!

09:49.770 --> 09:54.690
<i>between Tokyo's Toho Academy and Nara's Matsukami MS!</i>

09:51.650 --> 09:54.690
Go! Go! Matsukami! Get behind them!

09:54.690 --> 09:57.700
<i>The score is still at a deadlock at 0-0 even in this second half.</i>

09:57.700 --> 10:03.200
<i>Along with Nankatsu MS, Toho Academy are one of the contenders for the champion's title in this tournament.</i>

10:03.200 --> 10:08.290
<i>Despite controlling the game so far, their scoring power isn't enough, and the game remains scoreless.</i>

10:08.290 --> 10:10.690
<i>Their ace's absence does show.</i>

10:10.690 --> 10:15.970
<i>Kojiro Hyuga is simply sitting on the bench and has yet to set his foot on the pitch.</i>

10:16.650 --> 10:17.670
<i>Is it an injury?</i>

10:17.670 --> 10:22.220
<i>Or are they resting him for now while letting the younger players gain experience, like in the prelims?</i>

10:22.220 --> 10:25.500
<i>Some unexpected events took place before the tournament,</i>

10:25.500 --> 10:28.210
<i>but we still don't know the full details.</i>

10:28.210 --> 10:29.480
Brother...

10:29.480 --> 10:32.020
Kojiro's not playing.

10:32.020 --> 10:35.780
<i>For now, Hyuga is observing the game from the bench.</i>

10:35.780 --> 10:40.240
<i>Their opponent Matsukami MS are known for their defense, and have been persistent thus far.</i>

10:40.240 --> 10:43.370
<i>They leave no ground for Toho.</i>

10:44.600 --> 10:46.870
<i>They just stole the ball!</i>

10:46.870 --> 10:49.800
There's no way we'd lose to Toho when Hyuga's not playing.

10:49.800 --> 10:52.380
We'll score the first goal and drag Hyuga onto the pitch!

10:52.380 --> 10:54.750
<i>Time for Matsukami's counter-attack!</i>

10:54.750 --> 10:56.090
Go!

10:56.090 --> 10:56.840
All right!

10:56.840 --> 11:00.340
<i>Goalkeeper Wakashimazu tightly catches the ball!</i>

11:00.810 --> 11:02.990
<i>He's the #1 middle school keeper for a reason.</i>

11:02.990 --> 11:05.070
<i>He won't easily yield a goal.</i>

11:05.070 --> 11:06.350
Okay, Takeshi!

11:08.730 --> 11:11.310
<i>Now it's Toho's turn to counter-attack!</i>

11:11.310 --> 11:12.310
Sorimachi!

11:12.310 --> 11:13.110
That's the place!

11:15.920 --> 11:17.510
<i>He did it!</i>

11:17.510 --> 11:21.730
<i>A perfect shot from Sorimachi, who is playing instead of Hyuga in this one-top formation!</i>

11:21.730 --> 11:26.490
<i>And Sawada sent a superb cross his way. That was a textbook assist!</i>

11:27.920 --> 11:31.150
Well, even when Hyuga's not playing, Toho is simply strong.

11:31.150 --> 11:32.050
What do I write?

11:32.050 --> 11:33.750
That they're saving Hyuga for later?

11:33.750 --> 11:35.590
Or should I go with the injury story?

11:35.590 --> 11:41.210
Ever since Coach Kitazume said that he wouldn't be using Hyuga, he's kept going "no comment".

11:41.210 --> 11:45.970
Not much we can do. Maybe we should just put Sorimachi, Sawada and Wakashimazu in the headline.

11:47.850 --> 11:53.120
<i>Coach says that he won't let Hyuga play, but we can't become champions without him.</i>

11:53.120 --> 11:55.900
<i>Particularly, we can't beat Nankatsu.</i>

11:56.870 --> 11:58.150
<i>For now, let's get to the finals.</i>

11:58.690 --> 12:03.660
<i>We have to keep winning with our own strength without our captain until then.</i>

12:17.720 --> 12:20.590
<i>Toho Academy attacks once again!</i>

12:20.590 --> 12:21.450
Let's score again!

12:21.450 --> 12:22.340
Yeah!

12:22.340 --> 12:24.590
<i>A perfect pass from Sawada.</i>

12:24.590 --> 12:27.600
<i>Sorimachi traps it with his chest and...</i>

12:28.750 --> 12:29.720
<i>he shoots!</i>

12:31.640 --> 12:33.640
W-what?!

12:48.660 --> 12:50.160
<i>Goal!</i>

12:50.160 --> 12:52.830
<i>Toho Academy easily scores their second goal.</i>

12:52.830 --> 12:54.160
<i>The score's 2-0!</i>

12:55.280 --> 12:57.170
Hey, did you get that?

12:57.170 --> 12:59.840
Of course! Sorimachi's second goal, right?

12:59.840 --> 13:01.300
You idiot, not that one!

13:01.300 --> 13:03.300
I was talking about Hyuga's shot!

13:03.300 --> 13:03.590
What?

13:13.980 --> 13:16.440
I'm going back to the club house.

13:18.520 --> 13:20.010
<i>Hyuga...</i>

13:28.030 --> 13:32.540
— SAITAMA WORLD STADIUM —

13:29.410 --> 13:32.540
<i>It's the second day of the National Middle School Football Tournament.</i>

13:32.540 --> 13:36.540
— BAY COAST STADIUM —

13:33.110 --> 13:38.220
<i>The first matches of the tournament are being held at each stadium since early this morning.</i>

13:41.630 --> 13:45.470
They said Hyuga went missing, but it just looks like he's riding the bench for now.

13:45.470 --> 13:48.780
Rumor has it that he might be injured.

13:48.780 --> 13:51.410
Nankatsu had a rough time yesterday, didn't they?

13:51.410 --> 13:54.850
I heard that Soda of the Azumachi MS did a great job.

13:54.850 --> 13:56.190
Now shoot it!

13:57.480 --> 14:00.090
Is Tsubasa's leg okay?

14:00.090 --> 14:03.820
I just hope it will somehow work out after he rests today.

14:03.820 --> 14:04.640
Yeah.

14:04.640 --> 14:06.900
All we can do is pray that it will work out.

14:07.850 --> 14:10.490
But man, Tsubasa is sure cold.

14:10.490 --> 14:14.160
To think he'd keep his leg's condition hidden from us...

14:14.160 --> 14:16.030
Yeah, you said it.

14:16.030 --> 14:17.000
Now, now.

14:17.000 --> 14:21.980
Tsubasa was being considerate; he didn't want us to worry in the middle of the match.

14:21.980 --> 14:23.750
I know that much, but...

14:23.750 --> 14:28.630
Now we have another reason to try and not burden him any more than we already do.

14:28.630 --> 14:32.020
It's our turn to do the work.

14:32.020 --> 14:33.940
Yeah, you are right.

14:33.940 --> 14:34.640
All right!

14:34.640 --> 14:39.670
Let's get Nankatsu's third victory with our strength!

14:39.670 --> 14:40.650
Yeah!

14:41.730 --> 14:45.690
<i>Tsubasa being injured actually helped them boost their morale.</i>

14:46.790 --> 14:48.290
Yup, it is all good.

14:48.290 --> 14:50.450
There are no problems with the bone.

14:50.450 --> 14:53.020
How is your leg doing now?

14:53.020 --> 14:56.700
After a day of rest, the pain really isn't much.

14:56.700 --> 14:59.620
It was indeed a mild sprain.

14:59.620 --> 15:03.570
But as you've said, it looks like your leg tends to catch this kind of injury,

15:03.570 --> 15:05.160
so be careful about that.

15:05.160 --> 15:05.960
Sure.

15:05.960 --> 15:09.970
You should play your next match with taping applied.

15:09.970 --> 15:14.520
Do not force yourself today and take a break from practice.

15:14.520 --> 15:15.720
Understood.

15:15.720 --> 15:17.920
Take care.

15:17.920 --> 15:20.350
Thank you very much, sir.

15:20.350 --> 15:21.980
Thanks a lot.

15:23.460 --> 15:27.480
Whew, no matter how many times I visit, I am still not fond of hospitals.

15:27.480 --> 15:30.250
Wasn't that great though, Tsubasa?

15:30.250 --> 15:31.780
It wasn't anything serious.

15:31.780 --> 15:32.660
Yup.

15:32.660 --> 15:38.510
During such a time, not being able to play in matches due to injury as the captain would be disastrous.

15:38.510 --> 15:41.120
You all worked so hard after all.

15:41.120 --> 15:44.630
It's all thanks to your efforts, manager.

15:44.630 --> 15:47.880
Now you are saying things you don't even believe.

15:47.880 --> 15:50.880
damn tsu, you should've "ieie"

15:53.250 --> 15:54.640
Such a big park.

15:54.640 --> 15:58.270
It's Sunday today, so there are lots of people.

16:17.820 --> 16:21.800
Oh, I know! If I can't practice today anyway, we should go watch the matches

16:21.800 --> 16:25.790
between Nishikigaoka MS and Ozusan MS, and see who our next opponent might be next match.

16:26.240 --> 16:28.450
Manabu has gone to scout, anyway.

16:28.450 --> 16:31.510
If we hurry, we might even be able to see Furano's match before that.

16:31.510 --> 16:33.260
Sure.

16:33.260 --> 16:34.530
Okay, let's go!

16:34.530 --> 16:35.110
Wai–

16:35.110 --> 16:35.760
Tsubasa!

16:36.670 --> 16:40.520
<i>Geez, running around with a sprain...</i>

16:46.120 --> 16:47.770
Oh, where is the captain?

16:47.770 --> 16:49.230
He's not on the pitch.

16:51.800 --> 16:54.570
Coach, Hyuga isn't here yet.

16:54.570 --> 16:56.140
Hyuga won't be coming.

16:57.350 --> 16:59.950
For 3rd graders, this is their last tournament.

16:59.950 --> 17:04.410
As Hyuga won't be playing in this tournament, he has no need to practice here.

17:04.410 --> 17:06.380
That's why I told him it's okay not to come.

17:06.380 --> 17:08.860
No way!

17:08.860 --> 17:12.440
Coach, we can't become champions without Hyuga!

17:12.440 --> 17:13.880
He is right, coach.

17:13.880 --> 17:14.760
Shut your mouth!

17:14.760 --> 17:16.720
Do you mean to defy me as well?!

17:18.510 --> 17:21.600
All you need to do is to follow my orders!

17:21.600 --> 17:25.620
Wakashimazu, from now, until the tournament is over, you will be the team's captain.

17:26.140 --> 17:27.120
Got it?

17:28.400 --> 17:30.450
C-Coach...

17:33.440 --> 17:34.960
<i>Hyuga...</i>

17:34.960 --> 17:36.960
You called?

17:39.620 --> 17:43.730
<i>He is surrounded by three near the end of the game, but he is not yielding the ball!</i>

17:43.730 --> 17:45.540
<i>What a great...</i>

17:44.320 --> 17:45.540
I'm back!

17:45.960 --> 17:48.300
Big bro!

17:48.300 --> 17:50.540
I hope you guys have been well?

17:51.020 --> 17:52.920
Kojiro!

17:59.080 --> 18:01.810
<i>Matsuyama keeps the ball all by himself!</i>

18:01.810 --> 18:02.470
That's the place!

18:04.470 --> 18:07.730
<i>Matsuyama draws his opponents' focus and makes a pass!</i>

18:08.540 --> 18:08.980
Take it!

18:10.250 --> 18:11.020
Good!

18:11.020 --> 18:13.500
<i>Furano keep connecting their passes.</i>

18:13.500 --> 18:14.860
<i>What brilliant teamwork!</i>

18:14.860 --> 18:20.380
<i>Furano's members are doing a solid job this year, having further polished their team play.</i>

18:20.380 --> 18:23.950
<i>It seems that they are blowing their gentle wind in this tournament too!</i>

18:24.610 --> 18:25.450
Captain!

18:32.500 --> 18:33.360
Yes!

18:33.360 --> 18:36.510
<i>Their captain, Matsuyama scored at the last part!</i>

18:36.510 --> 18:38.510
<i>It's 6-0!</i>

18:38.510 --> 18:39.810
They've done it!

18:39.810 --> 18:43.510
It was worth coming all the way here from Hokkaido.

18:45.900 --> 18:47.820
<i>The match ends here!</i>

18:47.820 --> 18:49.370
<i>It's 6-0.</i>

18:49.370 --> 18:56.530
<i>Hokkaido representatives Furano MS have beaten the Okayama representatives Sakucho MS, with their excellent teamwork!</i>

18:56.530 --> 18:59.150
<i>Furano advances to the second round.</i>

18:59.150 --> 19:06.080
<i>We can deduce from this match that Furano might be the third force after Nankatsu and Toho, squarely in the race for the championship.</i>

19:06.080 --> 19:10.700
All right guys, let's keep this up and take the championship pennant back to Hokkaido with us this year!

19:10.700 --> 19:11.540
Yeah!

19:12.410 --> 19:23.990
<i>The next match between Kanagawa's Nishikigaoka MS and Kochi's Ozusan MS will be held at 11:30.</i>

19:23.990 --> 19:27.760
Ah, looks like we didn't make it in time for Furano's match.

19:29.320 --> 19:33.560
Is your leg okay after running that much, Tsubasa?

19:33.560 --> 19:35.560
Oh, I just forgot about that!

19:35.560 --> 19:37.190
Oh, you...!

19:38.000 --> 19:39.200
There he is!

19:39.200 --> 19:40.160
Manabu!

19:40.160 --> 19:40.820
Huh?

19:40.820 --> 19:42.690
Oh, Tsubasa!

19:42.690 --> 19:44.280
How's your leg doing?

19:44.280 --> 19:46.120
It's all good.

19:46.120 --> 19:47.680
Nothing serious.

19:47.680 --> 19:48.830
Is that so?

19:48.830 --> 19:51.090
So how was Furano?

19:51.090 --> 19:53.090
Oh yeah, they were strong after all.

19:53.090 --> 19:56.240
They've gotten stronger since last year, for sure.

19:56.240 --> 19:59.200
They will be a big obstacle in our path to victory.

19:59.200 --> 19:59.840
I see.

20:00.240 --> 20:05.780
As for Nishikigaoka and Ozusan, they're opponents we can't be laid back against, whichever may advance.

20:05.780 --> 20:09.350
They won't let us win this national tournament so easily I guess.

20:10.330 --> 20:12.350
<i>No matter who I have to face, I won't lose.</i>

20:12.350 --> 20:16.110
<i>I will make my way through this undefeated and go to Brazil.</i>

20:16.840 --> 20:19.360
Tsubasa, what are you even doing here?

20:19.360 --> 20:22.500
Teacher's gone so far and given you such an opportunity....

20:22.500 --> 20:25.650
You two should have spent more time by yourselves.

20:27.110 --> 20:29.910
Oh! I detect Tsubasa over there!

20:30.400 --> 20:32.300
You guys came too?

20:32.300 --> 20:33.080
Yeah.

20:33.080 --> 20:35.080
Morning practice was over.

20:35.080 --> 20:36.790
We're here to do our part of scouting.

20:36.790 --> 20:39.050
So, how was it Tsubasa?

20:39.050 --> 20:42.090
Yup, everything was fine.

20:42.090 --> 20:44.420
We aren't talking about your leg here...

20:44.420 --> 20:45.940
You two were alone, right?

20:45.940 --> 20:47.720
You held hands at least, yeah?

20:47.720 --> 20:49.220
With Manager, I mean.

20:49.880 --> 20:51.500
So how was it?

20:51.500 --> 20:53.440
Were things good between you and Tsubasa?

20:53.440 --> 20:55.150
Nothing happened.

20:56.230 --> 20:59.450
My dear seniors, what are you talking about?

21:00.980 --> 21:04.490
All of them are so curious.

21:08.640 --> 21:09.240
Huh?

21:09.240 --> 21:11.500
You are quitting Toho Academy?

21:11.500 --> 21:14.330
I had a little spar with our coach.

21:14.330 --> 21:17.250
It seems my scholarship will be revoked.

21:21.300 --> 21:24.560
When that happens, considering that Toho is a private school,

21:24.560 --> 21:28.640
it will be like telling us poor people to quit.

21:29.320 --> 21:31.010
That's not fair, big bro!

21:31.010 --> 21:32.780
It's okay.

21:32.780 --> 21:37.520
After that, I will return back to the middle school here and I will work after I graduate.

21:37.520 --> 21:41.780
But Kojiro, you won't be able to focus the football you love this way...

21:41.780 --> 21:43.780
It can't be helped.

21:43.780 --> 21:46.680
My school football life will end in middle school.s

21:49.720 --> 21:54.090
I might not be able to put as much time into football as I've done until now,

21:54.090 --> 21:55.960
but I can play football by myself, too.

21:56.390 --> 21:58.820
I will play football while I work.

21:58.820 --> 22:00.460
Kojiro.

22:00.460 --> 22:03.940
<i>It's fine if you are trying to make me quit,</i>

22:03.940 --> 22:05.420
<i>but in return...</i>

22:09.980 --> 22:17.620
<i>In return, I will fight against Tsubasa and defeat him with this right leg of mine no matter what happens!</i>

22:38.830 --> 22:44.870
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.830 --> 22:44.870
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.870 --> 22:50.880
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.870 --> 22:50.880
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.880 --> 22:56.930
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.880 --> 22:56.930
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.930 --> 23:01.560
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.930 --> 23:01.560
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.180 --> 23:07.850
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.180 --> 23:07.850
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.190 --> 23:15.280
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.190 --> 23:15.280
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.280 --> 23:21.330
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.330 --> 23:25.790
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.330 --> 23:25.790
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.080 --> 23:33.420
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.080 --> 23:33.420
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.420 --> 23:39.470
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.470 --> 23:45.770
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.470 --> 23:45.770
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:50.110 --> 23:52.110
COMING UP, EPISODE 37:
SKYLAB HURRICANE!
